<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan yarn rates end mixed, seen rising.</title>
<headline>Pakistan yarn rates end mixed, seen rising.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates were mixed on Thursday amid a rising demand and may be pushed up in the near term by fresh export orders, dealers said.</p>
<p>Rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchants Association for a 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>				     Thursday     Previous</p>
<p>    Al-Karam (A.K.)	    465	    455</p>
<p>    Popular (Shabaz)	   435	    435</p>
<p>    Din Tex.		     460	    460</p>
<p>($1 = 40.62 rupees) -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
